>
  <KeyTakeaways
    items={[
      'Dry eye disease is a chronic ocular-surface disorder driven in large part by inflammation and an unstable tear film — not only by “not enough tears.”',
      'The eye already uses melanocortin biology: α-MSH helps keep ocular tissues immunologically quiet and protects corneal epithelium in models of dry eye.',
      'PL-9643 is an investigational melanocortin pan-agonist eye drop that applies that anti-inflammatory, pro-resolution arm directly to the surface of the eye.',
      'Phase 3 MELODY-1 met its symptom co-primary (ocular pain) but missed its sign co-primary (conjunctival staining); MELODY-2 and MELODY-3 are designed to show both.',
